    "summary": "Cloth: a single weft-faced strip of hand-spun and hand-woven cotton and silk. The warp is of white cotton while the weft is composed of bands of two shades of indigo cotton, through which run lines of white cotton, and and bands of imported magenta alaari silk. These are repeated with variants along the strip, creating alternating weft blocks of light indigo with white weft stripes, and magenta and dark indigo stripes with white highlights. The warp ends have been cut but are not hemmed.",
